{#
  partials/_canonical.twig — <link rel="canonical"> (config/bolt/config.yaml `canonical_template`).

  The URL comes from partials/_canonical.macros.twig, which also feeds og:url and twitter:url.
  See there why it is needed, and when to remove it.

  Named through @theme, like the config: Bolt also renders this template into a redirect it
  answers without rendering a page (?_locale=xx, a record in a locale its ContentType lacks),
  when the theme folder is not on Twig's default path yet (SKILL.md section 1.6).
#}
{% import '@theme/partials/_canonical.macros.twig' as canonical_url %}
<link rel="canonical" href="{{ canonical_url.url(seo.canonical()) }}">
